      "tree_id": "f495001b5ef781d4ddbd9c65e38f3f8f9c966522",
      "message": "Phase 3: cloud/ logging -- ack ids at INFO, a bus trace_id, the pulling bridge's version (#349)\n\nThird and last piece of the logging overhaul: `cloud/`, the deployed\nCloud Run service. Scope approved earlier in the same session: ack ids\nat INFO, trace_id via contextvar alongside the existing Cloud Logging\ntrace, identify the pulling bridge, no bodies at INFO.\n\n## Changes\n- **`cloud/handler_bridge.py`**: the `ack` op's per-message ids were\nlogged at DEBUG (discarded by default) -- the one case where turning the\nlevel up after the fact can't recover them, since the messages are\nalready gone. Now INFO. `roster` publishing (a real mutation) was\nDEBUG-only; now INFO. Every op line now carries `bridge_version`, parsed\nfrom the `User-Agent: agent-bus/<version>` header the bridge already\nsends and that nothing logged anywhere but the generic per-request\nheader dump.\n- **`cloud/rpc.py`**: the connector's `ack_message` tool logged nothing\nat all for the ids it consumed. Now `log.info(\"connector ack\", ...)` per\nid, matching `connector write`.\n- **`cloud/logs.py`**: a `BUS_TRACE` contextvar and `bind_trace()`, the\nbus's own trace_id (distinct from `TRACE`, Cloud's own per-HTTP-request\ntrace). A call site inside a bound span writes every record with that\ntrace_id without repeating `extra={\"trace_id\": ...}`; an explicit one\nstill overrides it. Used for `read` (the store lookup and the summary\nline share one bind).\n\n## Verified\n- No message body is logged anywhere in this diff -- checked directly,\nnot assumed: neither the bridge's nor the MCP path wires its raw request\nbody into the field the refused-request logger reads (`self._body`),\nonly the auth/webhook/drain paths do, and none of those carry a\nmessage's `text`.\n- `274 passed, 13 skipped` (267 before, 7 new tests), `ruff check`\nclean, `basedpyright` clean, all against this branch's own base (`main`,\nwhich includes #342/#343/#344/#346/#347/#348).\n- Not run against the staging environment -- offered as an option if\nwanted before merge, not done unprompted.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01HDN9cc11dDC6iDCaVtYyHr\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
